# Additional primary-claim profile: did:demos:agent:<64 lowercase hex>, Ed25519,
# from DACS-Standard #296 at 725fa78bd124a7adb65df27adee376d5d44a4bd7.
# This is a source pin, not a declaration of complete DACS conformance.
#
# Implemented and tested in this split:
# - BundleBinding BB-4 signature/member checks and strict SIG-6 envelope decoding:
#   test/bundle-binding-rules.test.ts and test/bundle-binding.test.ts.
# - BB-5..8 role-holder resolution, deterministic per-signer work limits and
#   indeterminate overflow/divergence: the same binding tests.
# - catalogBundleBindings and scanChain retain all supported BB-4-valid records,
#   regardless of signer. The unauthenticated bundle route pages persisted records.
#   test/catalog-binding-pagination.test.ts covers scan -> direct persistence -> HTTP.
#   The existing reindexCore accumulation still caps records at 32 per signer/job/role;
#   complete carriage through reindex/federation is pending integration.
# - canonical.ts guards its wrappers against lone UTF-16 surrogates in keys/values;
#   SDK NFC behavior and valid pairs are pinned by test/canonical-rules.test.ts.
#   Other SDK canonicalizer callers have not all adopted this guard.
# - Isolated matchesVetRequirement helper: required AND, OR within oneOf groups,
#   AND across groups, exact verified primary, per-scheme claim normalization,
#   verificationRequired decision gate, unconditional freshness, and unknown
#   parameters unmatched. It requires an explicit session recipe roster and
#   pre-authenticated results; every included result needs an exact live recipe,
#   allowed method and trusted signer, including results with validUntil.
#   Every required/oneOf member must declare a boolean verificationRequired;
#   VerifyResult shape is checked even when verificationRequired is false.
#   Unversioned requirements select the latest version in the supplied roster.
#   validUntil or exact-recipe defaultMaxAgeSec sets the authority window; wrapper
#   expiry/maxAge can only narrow it. See test/vet-claim-rules.test.ts.
# - Isolated recipe policy and historical snapshot resolvers:
#   test/recipe-policy.test.ts and test/recipe-snapshot.test.ts.
# - Isolated authenticateAuthorityAttestation adapter boundary: missing, rejecting
#   or throwing adapters fail closed; adapters must authenticate original proof/hash
#   scope, signer and validator epoch. test/authority-attestation.test.ts uses a
#   signed fixture adapter; it is not a production method-specific verifier.
#
# Pending production integration (these helpers do not constrain current session
# admission or identity tiers): historical IdentityBundle/challenge authentication,
# session recipeRegistryVersion snapshot selection, required-claim matching and
# method-specific authority-proof authentication. Current authority evidence is
# hash-checked; the standalone adapter is not wired into graph/tier derivation.
# Tier policy still accepts operator_gated/closed_data/bilateral without disclosing
# per-result availability. The isolated new helpers use a live-only profile.
# Native-payment inclusion/finality and exact event/instruction settlement keys,
# authenticated rail snapshots, delivery cleartext/ACL/grant verification and full
# agreement/listing conformance are pending; graph reference verification alone
# does not establish these properties. No DACS_RAIL_SNAPSHOTS adapter exists here.
#
# Other current limitations:
# - Only did:demos:agent key resolution is enabled for BundleBinding carriage.
# - Current listing/graph signature readers retain permissive legacy decoding;
#   strict SIG-6 decoding is currently wired into BundleBinding verification.
# - SDK canonicalization accepts only integer numbers. Fractional publication is
#   unsupported; the publication route does not yet validate all fractions itself.
# - Discovery filters revoked listings; it does not serve revoked tombstones.
# - Generated A2A cards infer an endpoint/HTTP+JSON transport from the hosting domain.
# - scan.ts classifies any HTTP 404 as STORAGE_NOT_FOUND without checking the node
#   error body; missing/non-public locators are terminal until replay. This is an
#   operational label, never authoritative BB-8 absence evidence.
# - Node ac8f45f02fc9c25082ce9b83595c2e3916b49c5a is a source/API reference only;
#   no remote deployment revision is attested by an RPC URL or successful read.
